ruan: 47-bit user address space (TTBR0 T0SZ_USER 17) on the 4 KiB kernel, ported from UniXNU-sheng
(zzzz-sheng-ipados27-bringup.patch: T0SZ_USER, TCR_EL1_KVA_ENTRY, native_user_pt_attr, pmap_apply_user_tcr), without
sheng's __arm64e__ condition. macOS libmalloc maps its xzone range groups VM_FLAGS_FIXED at 455..512 GiB, beyond the
38-bit (T0SZ_BOOT 26) TTBR0 range. Replaces ruan-user-va-clamp.patch (must not be applied with it).

User pmaps get an L0 root (256 entries, 2 KiB: the same sub-page root allocation as the kernel's L1 root); the kernel keeps
T1SZ_BOOT. The TCR gets T0SZ 17 with EPD0 set when a CPU enters KVA (start.s), and EPD0 is cleared once TTBR0 points at
the empty table or a user root. Also VM_USER_STRIP_MASK, pmap_user_va_bits and machdep.virtual_address_size follow T0SZ_USER.

--- a/bsd/dev/arm64/sysctl.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/arm64/sysctl.c
@@ -319,7 +319,7 @@
 virtual_address_size SYSCTL_HANDLER_ARGS
 {
 #pragma unused(arg1, arg2, oidp)
-	int return_value = 64 - T0SZ_BOOT;
+	int return_value = 64 - T0SZ_USER;
 	return SYSCTL_OUT(req, &return_value, sizeof(return_value));
 }
 
